{"name":"Anzac","hex":"#c68e3f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Anzac","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of ANZAC.","A hamlet in northern Alberta."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of ANZAC (“type of soldier”).","Short for Anzac biscuit"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Anzac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Australian and New Zealand Army Corps","blocks":[{"text":"The Australian and New Zealand Army Corps (ANZAC) was originally a First World War army corps of the British Empire under the command of the Mediterranean Expeditionary Force. It was formed in Egypt in December 1914, and operated during the Gallipoli campaign. General William Birdwood commanded the corps, which primarily consisted of troops from the First Australian Imperial Force and 1st New Zealand Expeditionary Force, although there were also British and Indian units attached at times throughout the campaign. The corps disbanded in 1916, following the Allied evacuation of the Gallipoli peninsula and the formation of I ANZAC Corps and II ANZAC Corps. The corps was re-established, briefly, in the Second World War during the Battle of Greece in 1941."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Anzac_Cove_encampment_1915.jpg/330px-Anzac_Cove_encampment_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_and_New_Zealand_Army_Corps"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Coloured_illustration_of_Anzac_troops_after_the_fighting_at_Gallipoli_during_World_War_I_%285681735081%29.jpg/500px-Coloured_illustration_of_Anzac_troops_after_the_fighting_at_Gallipoli_during_World_War_I_%285681735081%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Coloured_illustration_of_Anzac_troops_after_the_fighting_at_Gallipoli_during_World_War_I_%285681735081%29.jpg/500px-Coloured_illustration_of_Anzac_troops_after_the_fighting_at_Gallipoli_during_World_War_I_%285681735081%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Popular illustration of Anzac troops after the fighting at Gallipoli","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColoured_illustration_of_Anzac_troops_after_the_fighting_at_Gallipoli_during_World_War_I_(5681735081).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/ANZACstaff1915.jpg/500px-ANZACstaff1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/ANZACstaff1915.jpg/500px-ANZACstaff1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Group portrait of officers of the Australian and New Zealand Army Corps outside Shepheard's Hotel, Cairo, Egypt, March 1915.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AANZACstaff1915.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Chora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_monument.jpg/500px-Chora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Chora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_monument.jpg/500px-Chora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_monument.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Chora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_commemorative_plaque.jpg/500px-Chora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_commemorative_plaque.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Chora_Sfakion_1941_evacuation_commemorative_plaque.jpg/500px-Ch